invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_ifma_sign_model_test
reason: rsa_sign64.c's use_ifma reads CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA alone, so a
  signature runs its exponentiations on AVX-512 IFMA under a value whose
  caller never stated that the multiply runs in constant time, and the
  52-bit products of secret digits rest on no statement. Every byte stays
  right. bin/rsa_ifma_sign_model_test counts the kernel's calls and
  requires none from rsa_sign64_sp1 under a value with the IFMA bit
  without the multiply bit.

--- old
    uint32_t both = CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_MULTIPLY;
    return (cpu & both) == both;
--- new
    return (cpu & CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA) != 0;
